module gunbc.quarantine_probe_disposition


// WHICH MECHANISM HOLDS A QUARANTINE PROBE, DERIVED TOTALLY -- NOT "IS IT IN THE ROSTER".
//
// gunbc.explicit_witness_admission RECORDS that a witness is a known-red quarantine probe.
// Recording is not gating: the required floor decides a probe's fate through
// v2.workflow.floor_expected_red, and no relation between the two carriers is claimed by
// either of them. An admission row can therefore assert known-red while nothing enforces it,
// and the row reads as covered for as long as nobody joins the two by hand. That is the
// AUTHORITY-SUBSTITUTION failure mode (DESIGN recurring failure modes, gunbc#8880): fact F
// lives in carrier A, operation O is governed by carrier B, A is cited as evidence about O,
// and only the arrow between them is missing.
//
// THE LIVE INSTANCE THIS MODULE WAS BUILT AGAINST, and it is the reason the guard is a JOIN
// rather than a membership test: test.claim.legacy_test_behavior_disposition_acceptance_test
// legacy_test_behavior_unclassified_frontier_is_zero carried a known-red admission row and was
// PASSING on main. Nothing was red, nothing named it for removal, and the claim went quietly
// true -- the quarantine's own removal path (a rostered row that passes reds the build) never
// fired, because the row was never on that roster in the first place.
//
// WHY NOT THE OBVIOUS GUARD. "Every QuarantineProbeExpectRed admission must appear in
// floor_expected_red" is the version this lane was first given and it is WRONG, measured: of
// the 19 live rows, 6 are legitimately held by the route-gap machinery and 7 by the floor's
// long-home decline, so that predicate produces 13 false positives on its first run and grows
// one bolted-on exception per holder forever. DESIGN's own entry for this failure mode says
// the fix is never a broad guard joining every A row to B, because that manufactures exactly
// the entailment being invented. The question is not WHICH ROSTER holds the row; it is WHETHER
// EXACTLY ONE DECLARED MECHANISM DOES.
//
// THE MEASURED PARTITION at 967b5bc1b92 (origin/main), 19 rows, exactly one holder each:
// 5 FloorExpectedRedHeld, 6 RouteGapHeldNoVerdict, 7 NeverRunDeclinedByHomePolicy, 1 NeverRunDeclinedByLiveTreeRead,
// 0 NeverRunPathExcluded, 0 held by nothing, 0 held by more than one.
//
// AND THE LIVE INSTANCE ABOVE IS NOT WHAT IT LOOKED LIKE, which is the finding this module was
// actually built on. The lane's acceptance target was that the legacy row is PASSING and
// therefore stale. It is not: its entry declares ReadsLiveTree, so the floor DECLINES it -- it
// is never planned, never executed, and never in `passed`. Run directly
// (`claim_batch --entry dag/test/claim/legacy_test_behavior_disposition_acceptance_test.dag
// --function legacy_test_behavior_unclassified_frontier_is_zero`) it returns FAIL, exactly as
// its admission row says. The deduction that made it look stale was sound in every step except
// an unstated premise -- that a discovered identity is either planned or long-declined -- and
// the floor's own receipt line names three arms. Deleting the row on that reading would have
// discarded a live red control.
data quarantine_probe_disposition_authority_note: String = "The total disposition join over gunbc.explicit_witness_admission rows whose cadence is QuarantineProbeExpectRed. It answers WHICH DECLARED MECHANISM HOLDS THIS PROBE'S RED OBLIGATION, and refuses both of the ways that question can fail to have one answer: no mechanism holds it (the probe is not gated anywhere, so a green run says nothing about it) and more than one does (two authorities for one fact). Every fact it reads is supplied by the caller -- the rosters, the home prefixes and the path exclusions are all parameters -- so this module owns the DERIVATION and none of the populations, and a caller that can only supply three of the four axes says so by what it passes rather than by the fold quietly assuming the fourth."

// THE FOUR DECLARED HOLDERS, and the fold is total over them by construction.
//
// FloorExpectedRedHeld -- the identity is enrolled in v2.workflow.floor_expected_red, which
// EXECUTES it every run and holds its failure as agreement. This is the only holder that keeps
// the witness executing against its subject.
//
// RouteGapHeldNoVerdict -- the identity is enrolled in v2.workflow.floor_route_gap: it executes and
// reaches a host effect the hermetic route has no arm for, so it produces no verdict at all.
// A route gap is NOT the enrolled failure and the two rosters are different axes; a probe held
// here is held against a claim that never reached its subject, which is weaker than the arm
// above and is why the two are named apart rather than summed.
//
// NeverRunDeclinedByHomePolicy -- the identity's authored module name begins with one of the required
// floor's long-home prefixes, so the floor never plans it. The probe is not gated; it is not
// run.
//
// NeverRunDeclinedByLiveTreeRead -- the identity's ENTRY FILE declares
// `data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = ReadsLiveTree`, and the floor declines
// every site in such a file. This arm was NOT in the specification this lane was given, and it
// was found by reading the floor's own receipt rather than its model: main run 32553487573
// reports `offered=11812 routed=10439 declined_long=543 declined_live=830 — every discovered
// site is exactly one of these`, so the floor's decline vocabulary has three arms and not two.
// `v2.workflow.required_floor` describes this arm as staged for deletion and its own header
// records that an earlier revision asserted the deletion as DONE while the host still returned
// it -- which is exactly why it must be read from the producer.
//
// HELD IS NOT CHECKED, AND THE ARM NAMES CARRY THAT RATHER THAN A COMMENT. Every arm prefixed
// NeverRun holds a probe's obligation only in the sense that NOTHING RUNS THE WITNESS, so a
// green floor says nothing whatsoever about the claim. RouteGapHeldNoVerdict is the middle
// state: the witness executes but reaches a host effect the hermetic route cannot serve, so it
// produces no verdict either. Only FloorExpectedRedHeld means the witness ran and its failure
// was asserted. `quarantine_probe_verification_standing` derives that distinction totally from
// the holder, so a consumer asking "is this claim checked" never has to read prose to find out.
//
// THE HEADLINE MEASUREMENT OF THIS LANE, and it is a coverage finding about the quarantine
// system rather than a caveat about this fold: EIGHT OF THE NINETEEN live quarantine probes are
// held by a mechanism that means the witness never runs -- 7 NeverRunDeclinedByHomePolicy,
// 1 NeverRunDeclinedByLiveTreeRead -- and a further 6 execute without ever reaching a verdict
// (RouteGapHeldNoVerdict). FIVE of nineteen are checked in the sense the admission rows imply:
// the witness runs and its red is asserted every floor run. That is the number a reader should
// carry away from this module.
//
// NeverRunPathExcluded -- the identity's entry path is excluded from the floor's prepared subject.
// ZERO ROWS INHABIT THIS ARM TODAY, measured at 967b5bc1b92; and, separately, the .dag side has
// no readable authority to feed it, for a bootstrap reason rather than a modelling gap: the
// floor's exclusion list decides which modules ENTER the prepared subject, so a list evaluated
// from inside that subject cannot be consulted before the subject exists. The one list the
// floor consults is the Rust literal `floor_prepared_subject_exclusions` in `cli_run.rs`, whose
// own comment records that adding rows to gunbc.ci_layer_roots witness_exclusion_frontier had
// no effect at all. Mirroring that literal here would be a second representation of one fact
// (DESIGN section 3) that drifts silently, which is worse than an arm with no production
// producer, so the substrings stay a PARAMETER.
//
// THE TWO STATES THIS ARM IS IN ARE DIFFERENT AND BOTH ARE TRUE. Its inhabitant count over the
// live rows is measured ZERO. Its inhabitant count IN PRODUCTION is UNMEASURED, because no
// production caller supplies the list -- the witness supplies a fixture list, which exercises
// the arm's derivation without observing the live population. Unmeasured and zero are the two
// states this repository most often conflates, and this guard exists to refuse exactly that
// class of conflation, so it does not commit it in its own carrier.
//
// TRIGGER: when this fold acquires a production caller with access to the floor's own exclusion
// list, that caller passes it and the arm's population becomes measured. Until then the count
// is unmeasured-in-production, not zero-in-production.
//
// AND AN EMPTY ARM IS NOT A DEAD ARM. If someone later proposes deleting NeverRunPathExcluded because
// nothing inhabits it, the answer is that the fold must stay TOTAL over the disposition space:
// a three-arm fold would classify a future path-excluded row as held-by-nothing and refuse a
// legitimate exclusion as an alarm. Totality is the property; inhabitant counts are not.
type QuarantineProbeHolder =
    FloorExpectedRedHeld
  | RouteGapHeldNoVerdict
  | NeverRunDeclinedByHomePolicy { matched_prefix: String }
  | NeverRunDeclinedByLiveTreeRead { entry: String }
  | NeverRunPathExcluded { matched_substring: String }

// THE SUBJECT: one probe, named the way the floor names it.
//
// `module` is the entry file's AUTHORED module declaration, never derived from its path -- the
// two disagree in this corpus (src/v2/test/claim/manual/english_emit_add_test.dag declares
// v2.test.manual.english_emit_add), and a path-shaped guess would silently miss the roster it
// is joining against. The caller supplies it from the same declaration the floor reads.
type QuarantineProbeSubject {
  module: String
  entry: String
  function: String
}

// THE SUPPLIED FACTS. Four populations, four owners, none of them this module.
type QuarantineProbeHoldingFacts {
  expected_red_roster: List<String>
  route_gap_roster: List<String>
  home_prefixes: List<String>
  live_tree_declined_entries: List<String>
  path_exclusion_substrings: List<String>
}

// THE ALARM IS AN ARM OF THE OUTCOME, NEVER A STABLE DISPOSITION.
//
// `QuarantineProbeNowPassing` is what a probe held by nothing derives, and it names the remedy:
// delete the admission row, or reclassify it onto a mechanism that actually holds it. There is
// deliberately no accepting arm for this state. A `StaleButAccepted` would NORMALISE the exact
// condition the guard exists to expose -- the absorbing fallback in miniature, the deficit's
// frequency zeroed by construction so nothing ever ranks for repair -- so the type is
// structurally unable to describe the guard's own failure mode as acceptable.
//
// `QuarantineProbeHeldByMoreThanOne` refuses, and refusing is the ruled-correct answer rather
// than a false positive: two mechanisms holding one obligation is two authorities for one fact,
// and someone has to decide which actually holds it. It carries every holder it found so that
// decision is made against the evidence rather than re-derived. No live row exercises it today,
// so this arm is about the future rather than the present.
type QuarantineProbeDisposition =
    HeldByExactlyOne { identity: String, holder: QuarantineProbeHolder }
  | QuarantineProbeNowPassing { identity: String, entry: String, function: String }
  | QuarantineProbeHeldByMoreThanOne { identity: String, holders: List<QuarantineProbeHolder> }

// WHAT A HOLDER ESTABLISHES ABOUT THE CLAIM, derived totally from the holder and never stored.
// Three states, because "the witness ran and failed as declared", "the witness ran and produced
// no verdict" and "the witness did not run" are three different amounts of evidence with three
// different remedies -- and collapsing them into "held" is precisely the conflation that let an
// admission row read as covered while nothing enforced it.
type QuarantineProbeVerificationStanding =
    RedAssertedByExecution
  | ExecutedWithoutVerdict
  | WitnessNeverRuns

fn quarantine_probe_verification_standing(holder: QuarantineProbeHolder) -> QuarantineProbeVerificationStanding {
  match holder {
    FloorExpectedRedHeld => RedAssertedByExecution {}
    RouteGapHeldNoVerdict => ExecutedWithoutVerdict {}
    NeverRunDeclinedByHomePolicy { matched_prefix: p } => WitnessNeverRuns {}
    NeverRunDeclinedByLiveTreeRead { entry: e } => WitnessNeverRuns {}
    NeverRunPathExcluded { matched_substring: sub } => WitnessNeverRuns {}
  }
}

fn quarantine_probe_identity(module: String, function: String) -> String {
  concat(module, concat(".", function))
}

fn quarantine_probe_subject_identity(subject: QuarantineProbeSubject) -> String {
  quarantine_probe_identity(module: subject.module, function: subject.function)
}

// EXACT MEMBERSHIP, NEVER CONTAINMENT. Both populations joined this way -- the two qualified-name
// rosters and the entry-path list -- are keyed by full identity and joined by EQUALITY. A probe
// whose function name is a prefix or a substring of an enrolled one is NOT held by it, and a
// file whose path merely contains a declined one is not declined. Containment proves neither
// identity nor multiplicity, which is the weakness the exact-admission authority was built to
// remove in the first place, and it is why the two arms that genuinely are substring-shaped
// (home prefix, path exclusion) are matched by their own functions and carry what they matched.
fn exact_member(needle: String, population: List<String>) -> Bool {
  v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: population,
    empty: false,
    cons: fn(acc, row) { acc || row == needle }
  )
}

fn first_matching_prefix(module: String, prefixes: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: prefixes,
    empty: v2.std.algebra.Empty {},
    cons: fn(acc, prefix) {
      match acc {
        std.algebra.Cons { head: h, tail: t } => acc
        v2.std.algebra.Empty {} =>
          if module.starts_with(prefix: prefix) {
            std.algebra.Cons { head: prefix, tail: v2.std.algebra.Empty {} }
          } else {
            acc
          }
      }
    }
  )
}

fn first_matching_substring(entry: String, substrings: List<String>) -> List<String> {
  v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: substrings,
    empty: v2.std.algebra.Empty {},
    cons: fn(acc, needle) {
      match acc {
        std.algebra.Cons { head: h, tail: t } => acc
        v2.std.algebra.Empty {} =>
          if entry.contains(needle) {
            std.algebra.Cons { head: needle, tail: v2.std.algebra.Empty {} }
          } else {
            acc
          }
      }
    }
  )
}

// EVERY HOLDER THAT CLAIMS THIS PROBE, collected before any of them is allowed to answer.
// Deciding on the first hit would make the arm ORDER the authority and would hide the
// two-mechanisms case entirely, which is the one case the ruling says must refuse.
fn quarantine_probe_holders(
  subject: QuarantineProbeSubject,
  facts: QuarantineProbeHoldingFacts
) -> List<QuarantineProbeHolder> {
  let identity = quarantine_probe_subject_identity(subject: subject)
  let floor_held =
    if exact_member(needle: identity, population: facts.expected_red_roster) {
      std.algebra.Cons { head: FloorExpectedRedHeld {}, tail: v2.std.algebra.Empty {} }
    } else {
      v2.std.algebra.Empty {}
    }
  let route_held =
    if exact_member(needle: identity, population: facts.route_gap_roster) {
      std.algebra.Cons { head: RouteGapHeldNoVerdict {}, tail: v2.std.algebra.Empty {} }
    } else {
      v2.std.algebra.Empty {}
    }
  let home_declined = v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: first_matching_prefix(module: subject.module, prefixes: facts.home_prefixes),
    empty: v2.std.algebra.Empty {},
    cons: fn(acc, prefix) { std.algebra.Cons { head: NeverRunDeclinedByHomePolicy { matched_prefix: prefix }, tail: acc } }
  )
  let live_declined =
    if exact_member(needle: subject.entry, population: facts.live_tree_declined_entries) {
      std.algebra.Cons { head: NeverRunDeclinedByLiveTreeRead { entry: subject.entry }, tail: v2.std.algebra.Empty {} }
    } else {
      v2.std.algebra.Empty {}
    }
  let path_excluded = v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: first_matching_substring(entry: subject.entry, substrings: facts.path_exclusion_substrings),
    empty: v2.std.algebra.Empty {},
    cons: fn(acc, needle) { std.algebra.Cons { head: NeverRunPathExcluded { matched_substring: needle }, tail: acc } }
  )
  concat_holders(
    a: floor_held,
    b: concat_holders(
      a: route_held,
      b: concat_holders(
        a: home_declined,
        b: concat_holders(a: live_declined, b: path_excluded)
      )
    )
  )
}

fn concat_holders(a: List<QuarantineProbeHolder>, b: List<QuarantineProbeHolder>) -> List<QuarantineProbeHolder> {
  match a {
    v2.std.algebra.Empty {} => b
    std.algebra.Cons { head: h, tail: t } => std.algebra.Cons { head: h, tail: concat_holders(a: t, b: b) }
  }
}

// EXACTLY ONE, DERIVED FROM THE SHAPE OF THE HOLDER LIST rather than from a count compared
// against a literal. Zero and two-or-more are different failures with different remedies, so
// they are different arms; neither is a variant of "not one".
fn quarantine_probe_disposition(
  subject: QuarantineProbeSubject,
  facts: QuarantineProbeHoldingFacts
) -> QuarantineProbeDisposition {
  let holders = quarantine_probe_holders(subject: subject, facts: facts)
  match holders {
    v2.std.algebra.Empty {} => QuarantineProbeNowPassing {
      identity: quarantine_probe_subject_identity(subject: subject),
      entry: subject.entry,
      function: subject.function
    }
    std.algebra.Cons { head: h, tail: t } =>
      match t {
        v2.std.algebra.Empty {} => HeldByExactlyOne {
          identity: quarantine_probe_subject_identity(subject: subject),
          holder: h
        }
        std.algebra.Cons { head: h2, tail: t2 } => QuarantineProbeHeldByMoreThanOne {
          identity: quarantine_probe_subject_identity(subject: subject),
          holders: holders
        }
      }
  }
}

fn quarantine_probe_disposition_holds(disposition: QuarantineProbeDisposition) -> Bool {
  match disposition {
    HeldByExactlyOne { identity: i, holder: h } => true
    QuarantineProbeNowPassing { identity: i, entry: e, function: f } => false
    QuarantineProbeHeldByMoreThanOne { identity: i, holders: hs } => false
  }
}

fn quarantine_probe_dispositions(
  subjects: List<QuarantineProbeSubject>,
  facts: QuarantineProbeHoldingFacts
) -> List<QuarantineProbeDisposition> {
  v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: subjects,
    empty: v2.std.algebra.Empty {},
    cons: fn(acc, subject) {
      std.algebra.Cons { head: quarantine_probe_disposition(subject: subject, facts: facts), tail: acc }
    }
  )
}

fn quarantine_probe_dispositions_all_hold(
  subjects: List<QuarantineProbeSubject>,
  facts: QuarantineProbeHoldingFacts
) -> Bool {
  v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: quarantine_probe_dispositions(subjects: subjects, facts: facts),
    empty: true,
    cons: fn(acc, disposition) { acc && quarantine_probe_disposition_holds(disposition: disposition) }
  )
}

// THE SUBJECT SELECTOR. Cadence, not expectation: this guard is about the rows that name the
// quarantine-probe consumer, which is the population the admission carrier claims a known red
// for. The expectation axis answers a different question (which verdict is agreement) and is
// deliberately not read here.
fn admission_is_quarantine_probe(row: gunbc.explicit_witness_admission.ExplicitWitnessAdmission) -> Bool {
  match row.cadence {
    std.witness_admission.QuarantineProbeExpectRed => true
    _ => false
  }
}

fn quarantine_probe_admissions(rows: List<gunbc.explicit_witness_admission.ExplicitWitnessAdmission>) -> List<gunbc.explicit_witness_admission.ExplicitWitnessAdmission> {
  v2.std.algebra.fold_list(
    xs: rows,
    empty: v2.std.algebra.Empty {},
    cons: fn(acc, row) {
      if admission_is_quarantine_probe(row: row) {
        std.algebra.Cons { head: row, tail: acc }
      } else {
        acc
      }
    }
  )
}
